            "result": "Found 4 email(s) matching 'Sarah live music event last night' in drafts (showing most relevant):\n\n\n--- Match 1 (Relevance: 0.09009523193608918) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: conference@techsummit.com\nSubject: Speaker Proposal - AI Security Best Practices\nDate: 2025-10-05T13:20:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nDear Conference Organizers,\n\nI'm writing to submit a speaker proposal for your upcoming Tech Summit 2026.\n\nProposed Topic: \"AI Security Best Practices: Protecting Your Models from Adversarial Attacks\"\n\nSession Details:\n- Duration: 45 minutes\n- Format: Presentation with Q&A\n- Target Audience: Developers and Security Professionals\n- Level: Intermediate to Advanced\n\nAbout Me:\n- 5+ years in AI security research\n- Published papers on adversarial machine learning\n- Experience with enterprise security implementations\n\nI believe this topic would be valuable for your attendees. Please let me know if you need any additional information.\n\nBest regards,\nYou\n\n\n--- Match 2 (Relevance: 0.05181761206022835) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: hr@company.com\nSubject: Vacation Request - December\nDate: 2025-10-07T08:45:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nHi HR Team,\n\nI would like to request vacation time for the following dates:\n\nRequested Dates: December 20-31, 2025\nTotal Days: 8 working days\n\nReason: Family holiday trip\n\nI've ensured that all my current projects will be completed before my departure, and I've arranged for coverage during my absence.\n\nPlease let me know if this request is approved or if you need any additional information.\n\nThank you,\nYou\n\n\n--- Match 3 (Relevance: 0.039994136131545815) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: vendor@supplies.com\nSubject: Contract Renewal Discussion\nDate: 2025-10-06T16:30:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nDear Vendor Team,\n\nI hope you're doing well. I'm reaching out to discuss the renewal of our current contract which expires at the end of this month.\n\nWe've been very satisfied with your services over the past year. However, we'd like to discuss:\n\n1. Potential volume discounts for increased usage\n2. Extended support hours\n3. Additional service level agreements\n\nWould you be available for a call this week to discuss these points?\n\nLooking forward to continuing our partnership,\nVince\n\n\n--- Match 4 (Relevance: 0.03163392938438989) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: mike@enron.com\nSubject: Request for Additional Resources\nDate: 2025-10-07T10:15:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nHi Mike,\n\nI hope this email finds you well. I'm writing to request additional resources for the current project.\n\nCurrent situation:\n- Team is working at full capacity\n- Project timeline is tight\n- Quality may be compromised without additional support\n\nRequest:\n- 2 additional developers\n- Extended deadline by 2 weeks\n- Additional budget for tools and training\n\nI'd appreciate the opportunity to discuss this further in our next meeting.\n\nBest regards,\nVince\n",
